---@class cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParameters
---@field additional_cacheable_ports? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersAdditionalCacheablePortsList|distilled.Null A list of additional ports that caching should be enabled on.
---@field browser_ttl? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersBrowserTtl|distilled.Null How long client browsers should cache the response. Cloudflare cache purge will not purge content cached on client browsers, so high browser TTLs may lead to stale content.
---@field cache? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the request's response from the origin is eligible for caching. Caching itself will still depend on the cache control header and your other caching configurations.
---@field cache_key? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersCacheKey|distilled.Null Which components of the request are included in or excluded from the cache key Cloudflare uses to store the response in cache.
---@field cache_reserve? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersCacheReserve|distilled.Null Settings to determine whether the request's response from origin is eligible for Cache Reserve (requires a Cache Reserve add-on plan).
---@field edge_ttl? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersEdgeTtl|distilled.Null How long the Cloudflare edge network should cache the response.
---@field origin_cache_control? boolean|distilled.Null Whether Cloudflare will aim to strictly adhere to RFC 7234.
---@field origin_error_page_passthru? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to generate Cloudflare error pages for issues from the origin server.
---@field origin_range_requests? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersOriginRangeRequests|distilled.Null Controls whether Cloudflare fetches a large asset from the origin as a series of range requests instead of one whole-body request.
---@field read_timeout? number|distilled.Null A timeout value between two successive read operations to use for your origin server. Historically, the timeout value between two read options from Cloudflare to an origin server is 100 seconds. If you are attempting to reduce HTTP 524 errors because of timeouts from an origin server, try increasing this timeout value.
---@field respect_strong_etags? boolean|distilled.Null Whether Cloudflare should respect strong ETag (entity tag) headers. If false, Cloudflare converts strong ETag headers to weak ETag headers.
---@field serve_stale? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersServeStale|distilled.Null When to serve stale content from cache.
---@field shared_dictionary? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersSharedDictionary|distilled.Null Configuration for shared dictionary compression. When set, Cloudflare injects Use-As-Dictionary headers on matching cacheable responses.
---@field strip_etags? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to strip ETag headers from the origin response before caching.
---@field strip_last_modified? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to strip Last-Modified headers from the origin response before caching.
---@field strip_set_cookie? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to strip Set-Cookie headers from the origin response before caching.
---@field vary? cloudflare.rulesets.CreateResultRulesetRulesItemSetCacheSettingsRuleActionParametersVary|distilled.Null Controls how cached responses vary based on request headers. `default` is required by the API and applies to any Vary response header that does not have a per-header override.

